-- do not edit. It reads every table of the book's four schemas and changes
-- nothing. One row comes back:
--
--   loaded_with   the load file the database matches: through-q.sql (the
--                 small world) or through-s.sql (the year of history and the
--                 sales warehouse)
--   reset         no, or the load file to run to return to that state
--   changed       the tables that differ from the load: changed (rows or
--                 columns), missing, or not in the load (a table or view you
--                 created in the book's schemas)
--   simulation    whether the simulation's results, ksl_db, are there
--                 (chapter 12 adds them to dbconcepts)
--
-- Tables you create in the public schema, or in a schema of your own, are not
-- checked, and a load file does not remove them.

